cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite the accompanying paper using the
  preferred citation below and identify artifact release 1.2.2.
type: software
title: "Banking Audit Evidence: Reproducibility Artifact"
authors:
  - family-names: Dalli
    given-names: Angelo
    affiliation: UMNAI
version: "1.2.2"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility artifact for an executable banking-audit contract separating
  source grounding, policy execution and final-action attribution. Includes
  100 fictional episodes with 700 assertions, eight separate diagnostic
  episodes, a bounded checker, authored reference labels, archived model
  outputs and offline scoring. Results measure fixture conformance and
  preserve the distinct provenance of unmatched model procedures.
keywords:
  - explainability
  - claim verification
  - decision provenance
  - evidence grounding
  - banking audits
  - reproducibility
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: Dalli
      given-names: Angelo
      affiliation: UMNAI
  title: "Separating Grounding, Execution and Attribution in Foundation-Model-Assisted Banking Audits"
  year: 2026
